## Known fixes (GCE vs Colab)

| Issue | Fix |
| :--- | :--- |
| `unzip: command not found` | Notebook uses Python `zipfile` (no CLI unzip) |
| `libGL.so.1` / `No module named cv2` | `pip install opencv-python-headless==4.10.0.84` in venv (not 4.13) |
| `!pip` then `import cv2` fails | Wrong kernel; use **vst .venv** kernel; notebook uses `sys.executable -m pip` |
| `import cv2` OK but `!yolo` no cv2 | Kernel != `yolo` CLI env; notebook uses `YOLO().export()` API |
| TF `float8_e4m3b11fnuz` on export | Ultralytics upgraded TF; run TF pins cell; `YOLO_AUTOINSTALL=0`; **restart kernel** |
| `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` | T2 tunnel missing or Cursor browser; use Chrome + T2 |
| `gcloud scp` on VM | Run `scp` on **Mac** only |
| Zone typo `europe-west4-a--` | Single space before `--` |

### Repair venv on VM (if export stack broken)

```sh
source ~/vst/.venv/bin/activate
pip uninstall -y tf-keras tf_keras tensorflow tensorboard opencv-python-headless opencv-python
pip install tensorflow==2.18.0 tensorboard==2.18.0 protobuf==5.29.6 ml-dtypes==0.4.1
pip install tf-keras==2.18.0 onnx==1.17.0 onnxruntime==1.26.0
pip install onnx2tf==1.22.3 onnxslim==0.1.94 sng4onnx onnx-graphsurgeon
pip install opencv-python-headless==4.10.0.84
python -c "import cv2, tensorflow as tf; print(cv2.__version__, tf.__version__)"
# expect: 4.10.0 2.18.0
```

Then Jupyter: **Restart Kernel** → resume from TF pins cell.

